    "working_thesis": "Hannah Arendt examines the fundamental distinctions between labor, work, and action within the human condition, tracing how the modern age's elevation of the animal laborans and the triumph of a consumer society have eclipsed the world-building capacities of homo faber and threatened the stability of the human artifice."
